        {
          "name": "config",
          "item": [
            {
              "name": "Apply a config change",
              "request": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [
                  {
                    "key": "Content-Type",
                    "value": "application/json"
                  }
                ],
                "body": {
                  "mode": "raw",
                  "raw": "{\n  \"desired\": {\n    \"rules\": []\n  },\n  \"dryRun\": true\n}",
                  "options": {
                    "raw": {
                      "language": "json"
                    }
                  }
                },
                "url": "{{baseUrl}}{{apiPrefix}}/config/apply",
                "description": "Diffs the desired config against the current rules and applies it. A missing `desired` key returns 400; a plan with errors returns 200 `ok:false` (no mutation). `dryRun:true` returns the plan + applied counts without mutating (and is allowed even for destructive plans). A non-dry-run plan with destructive operations requires `yes:true` (else 400). When the plan has drift, the rules are replaced (MUTATING; enabled rules start). Unlike `plan` (always a dry-run) and `import` (a raw replace/merge), apply gates on drift/destructive/confirmation and returns the plan with an `appliedAt` timestamp."
              },
              "event": [
                {
                  "listen": "test",
                  "script": {
                    "type": "text/javascript",
                    "exec": [
                      "const documented = [200,400];",
                      "pm.test(\"Status is documented by the API contract\", function () {",
